From abb261871df2043ec5edee7e5ff2d1c42944b009 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 11:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] perf(dsv41): SP ratio-2 compressor projection and CED
 encoder-only chunks

Upstream base: candidate-54 vLLM patch series (patch head 4e8133ff10a125b90753c2727f162e29fe37f30c, tree 5f021d9a7f01c03e2389dd3d8021759cfa19ea34) plus #957 part 1 (the replicated BF16 compressor through TP4; tree 3959b21147bc9f98f4ebcd48e2c80e0f42d4e2ef).

Rationale:
1. On encoder layers 2, 8, and 14 (compress_ratio == 2), DeepseekCompressor._sp_enabled was restricted to compress_ratio == 1. During SP prefill, these three layers disabled _gather_front, gathered the full [rows, 5120] BF16 hidden state across TP ranks before attention, ran fused_wqa_wkv and fused_wkv_wgate on all rows on every rank, and performed an extra column all-gather for the compressor projection. Enable _sp_enabled for compress_ratio in (1, 2) using bf16_gemm_two(512, 5120, out_dtype="float32", shards=split["shards"], blocked=split["blocked"]) on sp_rows.local_rows and sp_rows.gather_many(local_values, local_gates), and enable _gather_front on layers 2, 8, and 14 so both the attention front and compressor project only local SP rows.
2. On multi-chunk prefill requests, non-final chunks ending at or before the CED decoder replay floor (start + q <= floor) select 0 real decoder replay rows (padded to 1 dummy row [0] solely to keep compact decoder tensors non-empty). Previously, the forward pass still executed layer 20's decoder attention and MoE plus all 19 decoder layers (layers 21..39) on that dummy row and ran two [rows, 5120] scatter_rows zero-fills. Track encoder_only on CEDState when every request in the step is a non-final prefill chunk ending at or before floor, stop at the CED boundary layer immediately after mhc.pre and prepare_global_kv, and return preallocated zeros.

Quality implications:
Lossless and bit-exact. bf16_gemm_two with shards=5, blocked=True reproduces the column-parallel fused_wkv_wgate split-K reduction bit for bit, and non-final prefill chunks ending at or before the CED replay floor have no selected decoder replay rows or sampled output logits.

Tests:
- pytest tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_1_compressor_prepare.py tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_1_compressor.py tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_1_attention.py tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_1_ced_model.py tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_1_ced_sp.py tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_1_sp_prefill.py (347 passed).

Upstream status:
Local DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash prefill optimization for GB10 clusters.

Round 3 rebase (candidate-56, after #957 part 1 on candidate-54):
The PR was written on 1107 (tree ed1bdb7a7684da33d403a055521ac0c4dd7ca670). Three base patches since then change the code it edits, so the rebase re-derives those parts; the PR's semantics (the ratio-2 SP compressor projection with the local attention front on layers 2, 8 and 14, and the CED encoder_only early exit on non-final prefill chunks) are unchanged.
- attention.py, #1009 round 1 (0778): _sp_front replaced the BF16 _gather_front (norms, copy_columns/split_columns, one BF16 gather) that the PR extended to compressor layers. The compressor layers now take #1009's local front: sp_attention_front writes the MXFP8 q cast and the 528-byte SWA records on this rank's rows, one grouped gather_mxfp8 carries them, write_swa_records stores the gathered records, and the index head weights stay rank-local in prefill steps (gathered in an SP decode step). forward_mqa never reads kv, so the front's kv=None is enough for compressor layers too. _tilelang_calls declares sp_front_call and swa_records_call for SP compressor layers (instead of the PR's copy_columns/split_columns keys, which no path launches any more).
- attention.py, #1012 round 1 (0765): the decode overlap (_can_overlap_decode, _forward_decode_overlapped) refuses SP steps, so the PR's SP global-KV call (_prepare_global_kv on the local rows with sp_rows) sits in the non-overlapped branch, beside the full-row call it was next to; the overlapped decode path (non-SP, full rows) is unchanged. _forward_tilelang's new gates argument defaults to self._gates, so the overlapped path's _finish_project + _forward_tilelang call reads the same buffers as before.
- ced.py, #960 round 1 (0788): CEDState.encoder_only sits beside the pinned host staging rings. stage_floors (the FULL-graph replay staging) leaves it alone: the model reads its flag only at the CED boundary, which runs only with compacted ced_indices, and those come only from _stage_ced, which sets the flag on every eager step.
- compressor.py, #957 part 1: through TP4 fused_wkv_wgate is replicated and unpacked (tp_size 1), so bind() reads the ratio-2 SP weight in place (the [1024, 5120] layer weight, no all-gather, no extra memory), and _sp_projection_call's bf16_gemm_two(512, 5120, shards=5, blocked=True, float32) is the very kernel the replicated layer's own prefill GEMM is, run on this rank's rows. Above TP4 the PR's gather-and-unpad of the sharded weight is kept (10 MiB a ratio-2 layer). The rebase updates the bind() comment and the sp_prefill module notes to match.
Bit-exactness (sp8, GB10; spark-ds41f:candidate-50 image with the trees mounted):
- tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_1_compressor.py::test_sp_ratio2_projection_matches_full_rows (new) binds the ratio-2 SP projection as serving binds it at TP2..TP8 and checks every rank's bf16_gemm_two on its local rows, gathered, against TP1's project_parts (each rank's own replicated projection through TP4; the sharded project_parts plus gather_columns_into above it) at 129 to 16,384 rows, with and without NaN/Inf rows: equal bit for bit at every TP. Through TP4 the SP weight is the layer weight (same storage) and bind() makes no all-gather.
- vLLM's own TileLang attention of layers 2 (ratio-2 KV, index and candidate source) and 20 (ratio 1) at TP4 and TP3 rank shapes on one GPU, the SP all-gather simulated across the ranks to a fixed point: whole prefills (4,096, 4,097 and 16,384 rows), a chunked prefill of three chunks (4,097 + 4,096 + 2,051 rows, caches and the ratio-2 state ring carried), decode rows beside a prefill, and SP decode steps (214 and 216 rows) give every rank the same attention output, top-k indices and SWA, main KV, index-key and state-ring cache bytes as the base without this patch, on two boots, with and without breakable graphs. Non-SP decode is untouched: the decode overlap and the full-row path are the base's.
- The CED early exit skips only the decoder rows of a step in which every request is a non-final chunk ending at or before its replay floor: one dummy row a request, replayed from itself, whose logits the runner discards and whose decoder and draft window entries lie before every later row's window (replay_rows, bind_draft_replay_start), so no later output reads them.
Tests (round 3): the PR's six files plus tests/kernels/test_deepseek_v41_tilelang_front.py, tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_1_prepare.py, tests/v1/attention/test_b12x_v41_ced_metadata.py, tests/v1/worker/test_gpu_model_runner_v2.py and tests/kernels/attention/test_deepseek_v41_ced_replay.py: 600 passed on two boots (the base: 582; the 18 new tests all fail on the base's code); two runner tests need conftest's workspace_init fixture, which the image cannot load (no tblib), and error at setup in both arms.
Own mark (sp8, one GPU, TP4 rank shapes, ABBA in one session, two boots an arm): a rank's SP prefill forward of layer 2, all-gathers as device copies (no fabric): 7.55 -> 5.93 ms at 4,096 rows (-21.5%), 15.80 -> 12.19 ms at 8,192 (-22.9%), 33.41 -> 26.06 ms at 16,384 (-22.0%), 73.09 -> 58.20 ms at 32,768 (-20.4%), 165.97 -> 138.06 ms at 65,535 (-16.8%); every candidate boot below every base boot. Each rank sends 7,992 bytes a row instead of 12,288 (the BF16 hidden state gives way to the MXFP8 q cast, the SWA records and the FP32 values and gates).
